# CODEOWNERS — Security Layer 1, Block 1 (SEC-01).
#
# Two paths in this repository can reach the client's live database. Everything
# else can be reverted; these cannot:
#
#   packages/db/supabase/migrations/   a merged migration runs against real
#                                      guest data, with no staging rehearsal
#                                      (see D1) — a bad DROP is not undoable
#   .github/workflows/db-migrate.yml   the job that pushes those migrations, and
#                                      the only place its secrets are read
#
# Requiring a named reviewer on exactly these paths is the cheapest control in
# the whole programme: it costs nothing on the 95% of PRs that touch neither.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ THIS FILE IS INERT UNTIL TWO THINGS ARE TRUE. Both are GitHub UI settings and
# neither leaves a trace in git:
#
#   1. The team/user below must EXIST and have write access. GitHub silently
#      ignores an owner it cannot resolve — a typo'd handle produces a file that
#      looks like a control and enforces nothing.
#   2. "Require review from Code Owners" must be enabled on the `main` ruleset.
#      Without it this file is advisory only.
#
# Confirm both by opening a test PR that touches a migration and checking that
# the owner is auto-requested. Do not take this file as evidence on its own.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Default: no global owner. A catch-all here would auto-request the same person
# on every pull request in the repo, and a reviewer who is requested on
# everything reads nothing — which would weaken the two rules that matter below.

# The two paths that reach live guest data.
/packages/db/supabase/migrations/   @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
/.github/workflows/db-migrate.yml   @KaguSoftware/tech-leads

# The gates themselves. Without this, the cheapest way to make a failing
# security check pass is to edit the check — and that edit would otherwise need
# no more review than a typo fix.
/.github/workflows/ci.yml           @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
/.gitleaks.toml                     @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
/.security/                         @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
/scripts/security/                  @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
/packages/db/scripts/check-*.mjs    @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
/packages/db/fixtures/rpc-allowlist.json @KaguSoftware/tech-leads
